    "chunk_text": "Selection of investors for the development of lands belonging to the Urban Development Authority\n\nPress briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-04-07 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)\n\n- The Cabinet has decided previously that the formal Procurement Procedure should be followed to select suitable investors when setting apart lands belonging to the Urban Development Authority on  long-term lease basis for the implementation of development projects. Accordingly, the proposals made by the Minister of Urban Development, Construction and Housing to follow the Procurement Procedures to select suitable investors to set apart the following plots of land, which have been transferred to the Urban Development Authority under section 6(1) of the State Land Ordinance, on long-term lease basis, adhering to the Planning Regulations of the Urban Development Authority, based on the valuation of the Government Valuer:\n\n* \tto set apart 03 plots of land with an extent of 42.03 Perches, 20.28 Perches and 20.72 Perches respectively, which can be further set apart after allocating lands required for the proposed urban development out of the lands acquired for the Sellakataragama urban development \tactivities, on 50-year long-term lease basis.\n\n* \tto set apart the plot of land with an extent of 03 Acres, 2 Roods, 24.59\t\tPerches from the land located in Dematagoda (537 Watta), on 99-year long-term lease basis."
